{title: City of Blood}
{subtitle: Ezekiel 22:1–31}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Word of the Lord came to me
Judge the city of blood now
Confront her with detestable deeds
Idols made against herself
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
You shed blood and bring guilt
Your days are near the end
Mocked by nations far and near
Princes shed blood with power
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are dross [F#]in the furnace
[C#]Melted [G#]by my wrath
[F#6]I will [D#m]gather you in[F#]to anger
And [C#]blow the fire [G#]of fu[F#6]ry [D#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Treating father and mother with contempt
Oppressing the stranger in your midst
Wronging the orphan and the widow
Despising what is holy to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Men slander to shed blood
Eating at mountain shrines
Uncleanness in your midst
You have forgotten me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are a[F#]trocious in the [C#]furnace
Melt[G#]ed by my wrath
[F#6]I will [D#m]gather you in[F#]to anger
And blow the [C#]fire of fu[G#][F#6]ry [D#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Prophets like roaring lions
[C#]Devour lives and seize treasure
[B]Priests profane my law
[C#]Officials like wolves tearing prey
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[D#m]I searched for one to stand
[C#]In the breach on behalf of the land
[B]But I found no one there
So [C#]I poured out my indigna[D#m][F#]tion
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [C#] [G#] [F#6] | [D#m] [F#] | [C#] [G#] [F#6] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] |
